  {
   "id": "r2",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "soul; of what good is an attempt to sink a well when the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "house is ablaze ?",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r3",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "77. In this world in which life extends over a few",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "winkings of the eye, we do not know what to do, whether we",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "should taste nectarious juice of diverse kinds of poetry, or",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "drink the streams of philosophy; whether we should modestly",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "lead a householder's life in company with a wife ennobled by",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "virtues; or whether we should dwell on the banks of the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "heavenly river, practising penance.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r4",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "78. These kings whose minds are as unsteady as a horse",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "are difficult to be propitiated; while we have a high ambition",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "and our heart is set on a lofty position, old age de-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "spoils the body and death robs ( one of the dearly loved",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "existence: (under these circumstances), O friend, there is",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "nothing advantageous to a wise man in this world except",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "penance.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r5",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "79. Pride being on the decline, fortune being dissipated,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "the mendicant having gone without gaining his object, the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "relations having diminished in number, attendants having",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "gone away, and youth having gradually died out, only one",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "thing ( lit. only this ) is proper for the wise viz. a habitation",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "somewhere in a brake in a cavern of the mountain, the rocks",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "of which are purified by the waters of the Ganges.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r6",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "80. Delightful are the moon-beams, and the forest spot",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "verdant with grass, the happiness arising from the company",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "of the good and of friends is gratifying; the narratives in",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "poetic works are pleasing; charming is the face of the beloved",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "shining with the tears deposited on it by anger; everything",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "is charming; but nothing ( is charming ) when the mind",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "is distracted ( see notes ).",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r7",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "81. Is there not a delightful mansion for habitation; is",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "not music &c. pleasing to the ear ( lit. fit to be heard); is not",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "the happiness of the company of one as ( dear as ) life itself",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "to (a man's) great gratification? But wise men have resorted",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
